856
00:00:49,471 --> 00:00:51,096
Hot damn!

857
00:00:51,264 --> 00:00:53,298
Look at all those girls!

858
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,725
Hey, Yohei!

859
00:01:00,273 --> 00:01:03,167
Where the hell have you
been hiding these girls?

860
00:01:07,364 --> 00:01:09,156
You devil.

861
00:01:16,957 --> 00:01:19,249
Hey, lend me your scythe.

862
00:01:20,418 --> 00:01:22,461
I'll cut three times your share.

863
00:01:22,629 --> 00:01:25,673
In return, we get
nice and friendly?

864
00:01:49,698 --> 00:01:51,156
Rikichi.
Yes.

865
00:01:52,367 --> 00:01:56,036
It seems the married couples
are the most productive.

866
00:01:56,705 --> 00:01:58,872
Time you got yourself a wife.

867
00:02:02,252 --> 00:02:06,422
Why do you always get so mad?
I just said you should...

868
00:02:07,632 --> 00:02:09,925
Katsushiro, go after him.

869
00:02:10,093 --> 00:02:12,219
Running off at a time like this.

870
00:02:13,388 --> 00:02:14,847
Rikichi!

871
00:02:15,849 --> 00:02:17,307
Rikichi!

872
00:02:21,479 --> 00:02:24,189
Shino, what are you gawking at?

873
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:43,500
What's this? A bear's den?

874
00:02:45,503 --> 00:02:47,671
This was done with a scythe.

875
00:02:49,799 --> 00:02:51,133
Was it Rikichi?

876
00:02:51,718 --> 00:02:54,219
Yes, though I didn't
actually see him do it.

877
00:02:54,387 --> 00:02:56,597
I lost him for a while,

878
00:02:56,765 --> 00:02:58,682
but then I spotted him
leaving this grove.

879
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:02,019
He was furious, soaked in sweat.

880
00:03:05,607 --> 00:03:07,274
What did you say to him?

881
00:03:07,442 --> 00:03:10,944
Nothing. Just that he should
hurry up and find a wife.

882
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:18,452
Something is upsetting the little
bugger, but he won't say what.

883
00:03:18,912 --> 00:03:21,330
You can see it
all over his face.

884
00:03:22,123 --> 00:03:27,711
Those lips of his are bolted
up tight as a house.

885
00:03:27,879 --> 00:03:30,297
Why don't you try to open them up?

886
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,697
Who is there?

887
00:03:38,765 --> 00:03:40,157
It is me.

888
00:03:42,393 --> 00:03:44,937
All clear?
Yes.

889
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:56,323
Have a seat.
Let's have a little chat.

890
00:04:01,496 --> 00:04:05,040
I think talking...

891
00:04:05,708 --> 00:04:07,584
is a good thing.

892
00:04:08,128 --> 00:04:12,172
Whatever your burden may be,
talking can ease it.

893
00:04:15,343 --> 00:04:19,263
You, for example,
seem pretty tight-lipped,

894
00:04:19,681 --> 00:04:24,393
but if you're suffering,
you shouldn't bottle it up.

895
00:04:27,147 --> 00:04:31,692
Letting out your feelings
bit by bit can work wonders.

896
00:04:32,902 --> 00:04:35,571
I've got nothing to say.

897
00:04:53,173 --> 00:04:55,048
Time to head out.

898
00:04:57,552 --> 00:04:58,735
Shall we wake him?

899
00:04:58,803 --> 00:05:01,013
No, let the kid sleep.

900
00:05:04,934 --> 00:05:06,393
Shino.

901
00:05:09,147 --> 00:05:11,231
I swear he just said "Shino."

902
00:05:14,235 --> 00:05:16,111
Sounds like a woman's name.

903
00:05:16,279 --> 00:05:19,114
Even kids can be charmers
in their dreams.

904
00:05:25,496 --> 00:05:28,040
Where shall we start our rounds?

905
00:05:28,208 --> 00:05:31,418
The place that worries
us most, of course.

906
00:06:28,768 --> 00:06:30,269
Who is there?

907
00:06:37,068 --> 00:06:38,610
Who is there?

908
00:06:39,153 --> 00:06:40,821
Come out here!

909
00:06:41,531 --> 00:06:42,631
Who is there?

910
00:06:42,699 --> 00:06:44,157
Kikuchiyo.

911
00:06:46,494 --> 00:06:48,578
You are lucky it was us.

912
00:06:48,955 --> 00:06:52,124
If we'd been bandits,
you'd be headless right now.

913
00:07:24,115 --> 00:07:25,657
Yohei.

914
00:07:27,035 --> 00:07:28,744
What's this?

915
00:07:29,037 --> 00:07:31,163
That's my horse, sir.

916
00:07:33,458 --> 00:07:36,293
I thought it was a big old mouse.

917
00:08:15,917 --> 01:-52:20,003
The sparrows chirp, chirp.

918
00:08:20,922 --> 01:-52:24,758
The crows caw, caw.

919
00:08:28,554 --> 01:-52:31,848
I wonder why the
bandits aren't coming.

920
00:08:34,143 --> 01:-52:39,606
What a waste if they don't.
Think how much we feed those samurai.

921
00:08:39,774 --> 01:-52:43,568
Idiot!
It is best if they don't come!

922
00:08:50,118 --> 01:-52:53,370
A nag like that can't
carry your weight!

923
00:08:53,538 --> 01:-52:56,632
Yohei's horse is too worn out.

924
00:08:58,918 --> 01:-51:02,045
Please stop. Yohei'll be in
tears if you break its leg.

925
00:09:02,213 --> 01:-51:05,799
A skilled horseman can make
even a nag soar into the sky.

926
00:09:17,770 --> 01:-51:19,020
Not bad.

927
00:09:34,745 --> 01:-51:36,705
Very fine indeed!

928
00:10:00,688 --> 01:-50:02,772
They seem to be having fun.

929
00:10:04,317 --> 01:-50:07,194
The threshing is done,
and still no bandits.

930
00:10:07,612 --> 01:-50:11,031
Everyone is saying they
might not come after all.

931
00:10:12,241 --> 01:-50:14,534
A tempting thought.

932
00:10:15,036 --> 01:-50:20,248
But when you think you are safe is
precisely when you are most vulnerable.

933
00:10:21,542 --> 01:-50:23,960
Send them back to their posts.

934
00:10:57,411 --> 01:-49:01,164
I wish I'd been born
into a samurai family.

935
00:11:04,252 --> 01:-49:06,253
A farmer's life is too cruel.

936
00:11:07,338 --> 01:-49:10,423
My life has been so easy,
I'm ashamed.

937
00:11:10,591 --> 01:-49:12,926
That's not what I meant.

938
00:11:13,261 --> 01:-49:17,264
It is because you are a
samurai and I'm a farmer.

939
00:11:17,932 --> 01:-49:19,391
But I don't.

940
00:11:19,559 --> 01:-49:22,811
It is all right. I don't mind.
We can't know

941
00:11:22,979 --> 01:-49:25,088
what the future holds!

942
00:11:58,472 --> 01:-48:01,225
Coward! Act like a samurai!

943
00:13:08,751 --> 01:-47:11,544
Three suspicious characters
on the western road.

944
00:13:13,964 --> 01:-47:16,758
The villagers haven't noticed?
Not yet.

945
00:13:16,926 --> 01:-47:19,210
We can't have them
sounding the alarm.

946
00:13:21,389 --> 01:-47:24,307
I saw three horses
up in the hills.

947
00:13:24,475 --> 01:-47:27,494
I think they are bandits.
We know.

948
00:13:32,066 --> 01:-47:34,417
So they are here.
How did you know?

949
00:13:34,485 --> 01:-47:37,696
How could I not? This one
here was in such a panic.

950
00:13:41,075 --> 01:-47:43,743
Where are they coming from?
The mountains or the west?

951
00:13:46,080 --> 01:-47:47,580
The west.

952
00:13:56,257 --> 01:-47:57,532
Bandits!

953
00:14:01,637 --> 01:-46:04,764
Send everyone to their houses.
There are only three of them.

954
00:14:04,932 --> 01:-46:07,726
Tell them to keep quiet
no matter what.

955
00:14:07,893 --> 01:-46:12,272
They are probably scouts.
We can't let them see any samurai.

956
00:14:29,457 --> 01:-46:31,624
What is it?

957
00:14:32,001 --> 01:-46:33,793
Bandits?

958
00:14:36,464 --> 01:-46:39,507
Bandits?
Where are they?

959
00:14:51,145 --> 01:-46:52,479
Quiet!

960
00:14:54,482 --> 01:-46:56,357
Where are they, Shichiroji?

961
00:14:56,525 --> 01:-46:59,277
Beyond the fence.

962
00:15:13,667 --> 01:-45:16,252
No doubt about it.
They are scouts.

963
00:15:16,754 --> 01:-45:18,871
The fence took them by surprise.

964
00:15:19,757 --> 01:-45:22,275
They don't seem to
realize we are here.

965
00:15:22,343 --> 01:-45:25,470
With luck they'll report
there are only farmers here.

966
00:15:27,014 --> 01:-45:29,599
Hey, where is everyone?

967
00:15:29,767 --> 01:-45:31,476
That idiot!

968
00:15:32,520 --> 01:-45:34,437
Kikuchiyo!

969
00:15:40,653 --> 01:-45:43,029
Hey, I hear the bandits are here.

970
00:15:44,363 --> 01:-45:45,555
You fool.

971
00:15:45,658 --> 01:-45:47,992
Too late.
They've seen us.

972
00:15:58,838 --> 01:-44:02,382
If they report back that samurai
are here, we are finished.

973
00:16:02,952 --> 01:-44:06,021
I'll kill them.
The mountain is my territory.

974
00:16:06,679 --> 01:-44:07,820
I was just...

975
00:16:07,888 --> 01:-44:11,683
Enough. You can make up
for it by getting one.

976
00:16:11,851 --> 01:-44:13,226
Head them off at...

977
00:16:13,394 --> 01:-44:16,271
I know, at their horses.
Take us there.

978
00:16:17,398 --> 01:-44:19,023
Katsushiro!

979
00:16:19,859 --> 01:-44:22,402
Just watch, you understand?

980
00:16:29,451 --> 01:-44:31,661
Those are some horses!

981
00:16:36,458 --> 01:-44:38,376
Wait in this hollow.

982
00:16:47,261 --> 01:-44:49,971
What do you plan to do?
Who, me?

983
00:18:50,384 --> 01:-42:52,552
Katsushiro.

984
00:18:53,387 --> 01:-42:55,596
You can come out now.

985
00:18:58,892 --> 01:-41:00,768
Help me!

986
00:19:19,830 --> 01:-41:21,581
Back off!

987
00:19:22,590 --> 01:-41:26,785
He is a captive who has confessed.
He s begging for his life.

988
00:19:27,337 --> 01:-41:30,798
You can't just chop him to pieces.

989
00:19:32,092 --> 01:-41:33,342
Stay out of this!

990
00:19:35,095 --> 01:-41:37,305
Let me do it! Scum!

991
00:19:55,365 --> 01:-41:57,158
All right.

992
00:19:57,618 --> 01:-40:00,286
Let her avenge her son's death.

993
00:20:02,581 --> 01:-40:05,333
Someone help her!

994
00:20:05,501 --> 01:-40:07,126
I'll do it!

995
00:20:15,969 --> 01:-40:19,764
That bandit said their fort...
It is hardly a fort.

996
00:20:19,932 --> 01:-40:23,810
It is full of holes,
like Yohei's underwear.

997
00:20:23,977 --> 01:-40:26,312
Easy to sneak in.
Let's attack at night.

998
00:20:26,480 --> 01:-40:30,066
They have 40 men.
We'd usually pick off a few first.

999
00:20:30,234 --> 01:-40:33,194
Wait. We can't afford
to lose a single man,

1000
00:20:33,362 --> 01:-40:35,822
even if we kill five
for every one lost.

1001
00:20:35,989 --> 01:-40:40,535
War is always a gamble.
Three of us can take 10 of them.

1002
00:20:41,537 --> 01:-40:43,079
Rikichi.

1003
00:20:43,247 --> 01:-40:46,207
How far away is their hideout?

1004
00:20:46,375 --> 01:-40:47,875
At least a day.

1005
00:20:48,043 --> 01:-40:50,878
Hey, we've got
three of their horses.

1006
00:20:51,046 --> 01:-40:53,172
Half a day by horse.

1007
00:21:05,185 --> 01:-39:06,811
Very well. Let's do it.

1008
00:21:06,979 --> 01:-39:09,939
If we leave now,
we'll arrive before dawn.

1009
00:21:10,107 --> 01:-39:11,858
But who should go?

1010
00:21:15,028 --> 01:-39:16,195
Not you.

1011
00:21:18,907 --> 01:-39:21,242
And me makes three.

1012
00:21:22,119 --> 01:-39:24,036
They need a guide!

1013
00:21:24,204 --> 01:-39:26,622
There aren't enough horses.

1014
00:21:26,790 --> 01:-39:28,975
There is Yohei's horse.
You ride that.

1015
00:21:29,042 --> 01:-39:31,352
The only man to master that steed

1016
00:21:31,420 --> 01:-39:33,045
is Lord Kikuchiyo himself.

1017
00:21:42,097 --> 01:-39:44,307
Whoa! What the hell?

1018
00:21:45,142 --> 01:-39:47,251
It is the other way!

1019
00:21:49,771 --> 01:-39:51,647
Stupid horse!

1020
00:21:52,274 --> 01:-39:56,235
This way, you useless mule!

1021
00:21:56,987 --> 01:-39:59,572
You call yourself a horse?

1022
00:21:59,740 --> 01:-38:01,908
You should be ashamed of yourself.

1023
00:22:03,785 --> 01:-38:05,620
Hey, wait!

1024
00:22:07,915 --> 01:-38:10,751
Please stop! I apologize.

1025
00:22:11,919 --> 01:-38:13,419
I'm sorry.

1026
00:23:39,965 --> 01:-37:42,425
Hey, let's set the place on fire.

1027
00:23:42,592 --> 01:-37:44,610
Cut them down as they run out.

1028
00:26:18,832 --> 01:-34:20,833
Serves you right!

1029
00:26:21,460 --> 01:-34:23,210
We did it!

1030
00:26:25,672 --> 01:-34:27,631
Take that, you sons of bitches!

1031
00:27:10,634 --> 01:-33:11,967
Heihachi!

1032
00:27:32,781 --> 01:-33:34,515
Are you crazy?

1033
00:27:50,882 --> 01:-33:52,132
Stupid idiot!

1034
00:27:52,300 --> 01:-33:55,553
Look what you've done!
Who is she to you?

1035
00:27:56,930 --> 01:-33:59,165
She is my wife.

1036
00:28:02,852 --> 01:-32:05,004
Heihachi, hang on!

1037
00:28:44,811 --> 01:-32:46,478
You said...

1038
00:28:48,440 --> 01:-32:51,383
he'd be a treasure in hard times.

1039
00:28:53,236 --> 01:-32:55,613
The hard times have just begun.

1040
00:29:05,707 --> 01:-31:06,999
Stop crying!

1041
00:29:07,667 --> 01:-31:09,752
Damn fool!

1042
00:29:11,004 --> 01:-31:12,671
Stop crying!

1043
00:30:40,552 --> 01:-30:42,678
Goddamn!
Here they come.

1044
00:31:55,877 --> 01:-29:59,671
Take note:
They have three muskets.

1045
00:32:25,323 --> 01:-28:27,533
20 riders bound north,
13 south.

1046
00:32:27,700 --> 01:-28:29,868
Muskets?
Three in all.

1047
00:32:31,037 --> 01:-28:34,039
Take the south, and watch
out for those muskets.

1048
00:33:30,346 --> 01:-27:32,681
Retreat! Retreat!

1049
00:33:48,281 --> 01:-27:51,825
The 12 headed south have turned east.
Wasn't that 13?

1050
00:33:52,035 --> 01:-27:53,994
An arrow got one of them.

1051
00:33:54,162 --> 01:-27:55,746
Good old Gorobei.

1052
00:33:58,499 --> 01:-26:01,793
Make sure the eastern bridge
is out, and watch out for...

1053
00:34:01,961 --> 01:-26:03,503
The muskets!

1054
00:34:12,555 --> 01:-26:16,141
Take the north.
That's where we'll battle it out.

1055
00:34:17,101 --> 01:-26:20,562
If you knew that, why didn't
you build a fence there too?

1056
00:34:20,730 --> 01:-26:23,148
Every great castle
needs a breach.

1057
00:34:23,316 --> 01:-26:27,611
Draw the enemy there and attack.
You can't win by defense alone.

1058
00:34:39,332 --> 01:-26:41,800
Use your balls,
if you've got any!

1059
00:34:45,588 --> 01:-26:47,731
Take it away, damn it!

1060
00:34:51,678 --> 01:-26:54,388
Twelve riders are on the way.
Hurry with the bridge!

1061
00:34:54,597 --> 01:-26:57,307
Are you blind?
What do you think we're doing?

1062
00:34:59,227 --> 01:-25:01,645
And he said to watch
out for the muskets.

1063
00:35:01,813 --> 01:-25:04,055
What kind of idiot
you take me for?

1064
00:35:10,446 --> 01:-25:11,822
Where are you going?

1065
00:35:11,990 --> 01:-25:14,825
We are looking for Father.
We can't find him anywhere.

1066
00:35:15,118 --> 01:-25:19,705
Father intends to die in that barn.
That's what he's always wanted.

1067
00:35:25,420 --> 01:-25:27,587
Stubborn old fool!

1068
00:35:28,089 --> 01:-25:30,298
Hurry up and get him!

1069
00:35:33,886 --> 01:-25:35,929
Get out of our way!

1070
00:35:36,889 --> 01:-25:40,225
What are you doing?
Hurry up!

1071
00:36:01,998 --> 01:-24:04,332
On this mountain...
Twenty riders.

1072
00:36:04,751 --> 01:-24:07,035
And 12 to the east.

1073
00:36:07,503 --> 01:-24:08,820
Right.

1074
00:36:24,729 --> 01:-24:27,856
This won't do.
They're all scared stiff.

1075
00:36:31,694 --> 01:-24:33,178
Good! Again!

1076
00:36:34,864 --> 01:-24:36,248
Again!

1077
00:36:39,744 --> 01:-24:42,954
Shichiroji is at it.
Let's fire ours up too.

1078
00:36:44,457 --> 01:-24:46,166
Everybody out here!

1079
00:36:51,422 --> 01:-24:53,924
Raise your spears
and give the battle cry.

1080
00:36:58,554 --> 01:-24:59,671
Again!

1081
00:37:03,810 --> 01:-23:06,770
Damn them, listen to that!
We can beat them.

1082
00:37:10,650 --> 01:-23:13,318
Yohei, what's that look for?
Again!

1083
00:37:18,491 --> 01:-23:20,450
Take cover!

1084
00:37:25,164 --> 01:-23:27,040
Here they come.

1085
00:37:43,683 --> 01:-23:45,100
Goddamn them!

1086
00:38:21,387 --> 01:-22:24,314
Hey, where do you
think you are going?

1087
00:38:28,895 --> 01:-22:30,804
Oh, no, you don't!

1088
00:38:35,902 --> 01:-22:37,485
Don't panic!

1089
00:38:46,412 --> 01:-22:48,330
Goddamn you!

1090
00:38:52,919 --> 01:-22:54,377
They are burning.

1091
00:38:54,754 --> 01:-22:56,371
Damn bastards!

1092
00:39:26,452 --> 01:-21:29,237
Back to your posts, everyone!

1093
00:39:30,706 --> 01:-21:32,115
Dear!

1094
00:39:34,335 --> 01:-21:36,787
They are just rickety shacks.

1095
00:39:40,007 --> 01:-21:42,909
Everybody, back to your posts!

1096
00:39:54,480 --> 01:-21:56,022
Goddamn it!

1097
00:39:57,733 --> 01:-21:59,284
You dogs!

1098
00:39:59,735 --> 01:-20:01,920
That's the Old Man's house!

1099
00:40:04,865 --> 01:-20:07,575
Where is the Old Man?
What about that couple?

1100
00:40:08,035 --> 01:-20:11,037
And the little brat?
What the hell is going on?

1101
00:40:14,125 --> 01:-20:17,085
Stop!
You can't abandon your post.

1102
00:40:19,005 --> 01:-20:21,089
Kikuchiyo, come back!

1103
00:40:23,175 --> 01:-20:24,676
Kikuchiyo!

1104
00:40:39,859 --> 01:-20:42,652
Where is the Old Man
and your husband?

1105
00:40:52,621 --> 01:-20:55,582
She's been speared.
How'd she make it this far?

1106
00:41:02,048 --> 01:-19:03,965
Let's go!

1107
00:41:10,556 --> 01:-19:12,682
Damn it, what is it now?

1108
00:41:15,895 --> 01:-19:18,563
This baby... is me.

1109
00:41:19,065 --> 01:-19:21,566
This is just what happened to me!

1110
00:42:30,344 --> 01:-18:32,262
Here we go!

1111
00:42:40,980 --> 01:-18:43,064
What the hell?

1112
00:42:57,329 --> 01:-18:59,831
What the hell
were you staring at?

1113
00:43:01,000 --> 01:-17:02,584
Idiot!

1114
00:44:04,897 --> 01:-16:06,940
No one wounded?

1115
00:44:07,316 --> 01:-16:09,776
Good.
You did a fine job.

1116
00:44:09,944 --> 01:-16:11,611
Fine job!

1117
00:44:14,949 --> 01:-16:17,200
Gunpowder!
Take cover!

1118
00:44:27,711 --> 01:-16:29,420
Manzo!

1119
00:44:43,185 --> 01:-16:45,144
Where were you hit?

1120
00:44:45,646 --> 01:-16:48,815
Shino! Shino!
Bring me my daughter.

1121
00:44:50,025 --> 01:-16:51,442
Don't bother.

1122
00:44:51,819 --> 01:-16:54,737
If this kills you,
you'd die of a fleabite.

1123
00:44:55,948 --> 01:-16:58,533
You make a ruckus
over a little scratch

1124
00:44:58,701 --> 01:-15:02,579
and blow your daughter's cover
in the process. Nice going!

1125
00:45:31,942 --> 01:-15:34,193
You don't have to
chase them all down.

1126
00:45:37,656 --> 01:-15:39,699
That's far enough.
Well done.

1127
00:45:40,451 --> 01:-15:42,368
Who are you?

1128
00:45:44,246 --> 01:-15:45,997
Rikichi.

1129
00:46:00,971 --> 01:-14:03,514
They've attacked from
the east, west and south

1130
00:46:03,682 --> 01:-14:06,643
and run away each time with
their tails between their legs.

1131
00:46:06,810 --> 01:-14:08,561
This is the only approach left.

1132
00:46:08,729 --> 01:-14:11,356
We don't know if
they'll come tonight,

1133
00:46:11,523 --> 01:-14:13,650
but when they do,
they'll mass their forces here.

1134
00:46:13,817 --> 01:-14:15,526
Perhaps, but...

1135
00:46:16,195 --> 01:-14:18,279
I don't hear a thing.

1136
00:46:31,377 --> 01:-14:33,086
Nevertheless,

1137
00:46:33,837 --> 01:-14:36,172
this will surely be the
focus of their attack.

1138
00:46:36,590 --> 01:-14:38,549
I'll prove it to you in a minute.

1139
00:47:22,553 --> 01:-13:23,928
Good work.

1140
00:47:24,096 --> 01:-13:27,140
Now poke that scarecrow out
from behind those trees.

1141
00:48:01,675 --> 01:-12:04,802
I'd say tomorrow morning

1142
00:48:05,095 --> 01:-12:07,597
they'll attack us here with
everything they've got.

1143
00:48:07,765 --> 01:-12:10,683
And we'll let them in.

1144
00:48:14,605 --> 01:-12:17,774
Don't worry.
I mean we'll let one in.

1145
00:48:18,817 --> 01:-12:20,818
Two at most.

1146
00:48:21,820 --> 01:-12:25,490
Once they are in, we form
a wall again with our spears.

1147
00:48:26,200 --> 01:-12:29,076
The one or two who get
in are as good as dead.

1148
00:48:29,244 --> 01:-12:31,329
We can cook them up
any way we want.

1149
00:48:33,582 --> 01:-12:38,169
We'll pick them off patiently,
one by one, until the final showdown.

1150
00:48:38,337 --> 01:-12:40,379
Those muskets worry me.

1151
00:48:40,547 --> 01:-12:42,715
If only we could
get one of them.

1152
00:48:45,302 --> 01:-12:48,679
I'll go.
I swear I'll get one!

1153
00:48:48,847 --> 01:-12:51,766
No. You're looking to die.
I'll go.

1154
00:49:44,903 --> 01:-11:46,821
Footsteps! Listen!

1155
00:49:46,989 --> 01:-11:50,241
That's enough.
Get some rest.

1156
00:49:50,409 --> 01:-11:53,211
It is true. I hear them.
Listen.

1157
00:49:53,579 --> 01:-11:55,705
I said enough.

1158
00:49:56,582 --> 01:-11:59,709
You are exhausted.
Get some rest.

1159
00:50:02,462 --> 01:-10:04,171
I hear them.

1160
00:50:32,326 --> 01:-10:34,076
Two more down.

1161
00:51:09,071 --> 01:-9:10,279
What is it?

1162
00:51:13,367 --> 01:-9:17,495
State your business.
I'm going to get some sleep.

1163
00:51:18,956 --> 01:-9:22,458
You are a magnificent person.

1164
00:51:26,838 --> 01:-9:29,783
I've wanted to tell
you so for some time.

1165
00:51:56,868 --> 01:-9:58,419
They are here.

1166
00:52:02,708 --> 01:-8:04,709
We'll let one in.

1167
00:52:07,504 --> 01:-8:09,463
We're letting one in!

1168
00:52:16,888 --> 01:-8:21,392
Remember, after the first one is in,
jump out with your spears.

1169
00:52:40,287 --> 01:-8:41,537
Here they come.

1170
00:53:17,491 --> 01:-7:19,241
Step aside!

1171
00:53:21,787 --> 01:-7:23,329
Good work.

1172
00:53:31,046 --> 01:-7:34,131
What's wrong? You did well.

1173
00:53:34,633 --> 01:-7:36,550
Here he comes! Scatter!

1174
00:53:54,111 --> 01:-7:56,320
Fall back! Fall back!

1175
00:54:01,952 --> 01:-6:04,036
After them!

1176
00:54:12,337 --> 01:-6:14,004
Another on the way!

1177
00:55:56,316 --> 01:-5:58,067
Here he comes.

1178
00:56:14,292 --> 01:-4:16,126
Watch this!

1179
00:56:22,050 --> 01:-4:24,760
Having fun with your horsey?

1180
00:56:46,533 --> 01:-4:51,078
They've stopped.
Won't fall for that trick again?

1181
00:57:00,005 --> 01:-3:03,473
They are all wimps!
Who is scared of bandits anyway?

1182
00:57:10,098 --> 01:-3:15,352
That little skirmish just cost them four.
Kyuzo got two last night.

1183
00:57:31,953 --> 01:-3:34,204
That man is a true samurai.

1184
00:57:34,539 --> 01:-3:37,207
He is fearless,
his swordsmanship is amazing,

1185
00:57:37,375 --> 01:-3:39,084
and yet he is kind too.

1186
00:57:39,252 --> 01:-3:42,963
He never once boasted
about capturing that musket.

1187
00:57:43,381 --> 01:-3:47,885
He walked into a forest filled with
bandits as if on a mushroom hunt.

1188
00:57:49,262 --> 01:-3:53,557
Fascinating.
I'm not bored at all, I swear.

1189
00:58:11,409 --> 01:-2:13,327
Hey, Yohei.

1190
00:58:14,204 --> 01:-2:15,746
Take over for me.

1191
00:58:18,875 --> 01:-2:21,919
What's that face for?

1192
00:58:22,087 --> 01:-2:24,254
There is no danger here now.

1193
00:58:25,840 --> 01:-2:28,008
You make a great scarecrow.

1194
00:59:59,476 --> 01:00:00,767
Hear me good!

1195
01:00:01,853 --> 01:00:04,229
If anybody else turns yellow...

1196
01:00:10,403 --> 01:00:11,778
Out of my way!

1197
01:01:35,280 --> 01:01:36,530
Hey!

1198
01:01:40,285 --> 01:01:41,551
How is it going?

1199
01:01:41,619 --> 01:01:43,662
Man, they are a pain.

1200
01:01:43,955 --> 01:01:46,081
Won't be long now.

1201
01:01:46,499 --> 01:01:49,751
Everything is upside down.

1202
01:01:49,961 --> 01:01:53,797
They burn us out, and
we starve like farmers.

1203
01:01:54,632 --> 01:01:57,467
Quit your moaning.
There are better times ahead.

1204
01:01:57,635 --> 01:01:59,970
Do your part, man.

1205
01:02:39,677 --> 01:02:41,745
Hey, it is me!

1206
01:02:49,103 --> 01:02:50,854
Serves you right, you dogs!

1207
01:02:51,022 --> 01:02:52,022
Fool!

1208
01:02:53,191 --> 01:02:55,192
Why did you leave your post?

1209
01:02:55,360 --> 01:02:56,735
Just look at this!

1210
01:02:56,903 --> 01:03:00,530
Don't scold me, man.
My post is fine.

1211
01:03:01,366 --> 01:03:04,910
There is nothing heroic
about selfishly grabbing for glory.

1212
01:03:05,078 --> 01:03:09,289
Listen to me:
War is not fought alone!

1213
01:03:19,676 --> 01:03:22,719
Gorobei and Kyuzo, guard this post!

1214
01:03:28,101 --> 01:03:30,143
Let no one pass!

1215
01:05:38,064 --> 01:05:40,857
Stop, you asses!

1216
01:05:41,025 --> 01:05:42,734
Damn you!

1217
01:05:43,361 --> 01:05:45,362
Damn it! Two made it in!

1218
01:06:01,045 --> 01:06:04,089
Goddamn it!

1219
01:06:04,799 --> 01:06:06,383
Where is Yohei?

1220
01:06:46,382 --> 01:06:47,716
Yohei!

1221
01:06:49,343 --> 01:06:50,760
Yohei!

1222
01:06:51,262 --> 01:06:54,389
I defended my post.

1223
01:06:54,557 --> 01:06:57,225
Don't give up, Yohei!

1224
01:07:00,605 --> 01:07:02,439
Go ahead, shoot me!

1225
01:07:40,478 --> 01:07:42,187
Shichiroji, take over!

1226
01:07:53,449 --> 01:07:55,325
Gorobei!

1227
01:08:05,002 --> 02:-52:07,003
Gorobei!

1228
01:08:58,931 --> 02:-51:01,224
Just 13 left.

1229
01:09:01,809 --> 02:-51:03,852
But these last seven...

1230
01:09:05,104 --> 02:-51:07,230
came at a steep price.

1231
01:09:28,419 --> 02:-51:31,087
How are you? Tired?

1232
01:09:33,007 --> 02:-51:36,926
Poor man.
You've lost a lot of weight.

1233
01:09:41,098 --> 02:-51:43,641
I'll go throw some
water on my face.

1234
01:09:54,236 --> 02:-51:57,046
Next time they come,
we fight to the finish.

1235
01:09:57,114 --> 02:-50:01,367
It is better we fight it out
before we're spent.

1236
01:10:01,619 --> 02:-50:05,163
When do you think they'll attack?

1237
01:10:06,582 --> 02:-50:09,584
They are exhausted too,
and a few are wounded.

1238
01:10:10,002 --> 02:-50:12,128
They won't come tonight.

1239
01:10:12,296 --> 02:-50:17,509
But they have no food,
and their ranks are splitting.

1240
01:10:18,427 --> 02:-50:20,512
They can't afford to dawdle either.

1241
01:10:20,763 --> 02:-50:26,935
I say they'll come at us like
hell tomorrow morning.

1242
01:10:28,312 --> 02:-50:29,979
Katsushiro.

1243
01:10:49,458 --> 02:-50:50,959
An order from above.

1244
01:10:51,127 --> 02:-50:54,295
Place two on watch
and let the rest sleep.

1245
01:10:55,005 --> 02:-50:58,608
The men may visit their
families one at a time.

1246
01:11:00,803 --> 02:-49:02,445
So tomorrow is the showdown?

1247
01:11:04,348 --> 02:-49:06,558
Yes.
Please carry out the order.

1248
01:11:13,274 --> 02:-49:17,068
You all heard what he just said.

1249
01:11:21,073 --> 02:-49:23,291
I'll stand guard.

1250
01:11:24,118 --> 02:-49:25,994
The rest of you sleep.

1251
01:11:27,037 --> 02:-49:28,806
Manzo...

1252
01:11:31,000 --> 02:-49:33,042
you go home first.

1253
01:11:33,460 --> 02:-49:35,879
Take a good look
at your daughter...

1254
01:11:36,672 --> 02:-49:38,723
I mean, your son.

1255
01:11:47,933 --> 02:-49:49,225
I told them.

1256
01:11:49,393 --> 02:-49:51,561
All right. Get some rest.

1257
01:11:55,608 --> 02:-49:57,442
Katsushiro.

1258
01:11:58,903 --> 02:-48:00,545
How was Kikuchiyo?

1259
01:12:00,613 --> 02:-48:03,698
Still beside the grave.

1260
01:12:03,949 --> 02:-48:05,241
I see.

1261
01:13:18,565 --> 02:-47:21,401
Are we all going to die tomorrow?

1262
01:13:21,568 --> 02:-47:24,654
There is no way to know.

1263
01:13:25,281 --> 02:-47:27,824
But we might!

1264
01:13:50,055 --> 02:-47:51,472
Shino.

1265
01:13:52,099 --> 02:-47:53,766
Where is Shino?

1266
01:13:59,440 --> 02:-46:01,024
Anyone seen Shino?

1267
01:14:35,476 --> 02:-46:38,061
Sake?
Where did you find it?

1268
01:14:53,369 --> 02:-46:56,412
I see. They have stockpiles,
just like Kikuchiyo said,

1269
01:14:56,580 --> 02:-46:58,581
and tonight it all comes out.

1270
01:15:07,966 --> 02:-45:10,593
I think I'll help myself.

1271
01:15:14,306 --> 02:-45:15,890
Shino!

1272
01:15:41,667 --> 02:-45:44,752
Here is some sake.
Drink up and get some sleep.

1273
01:15:50,008 --> 02:-45:54,303
This is hardly like you.
You must rest for the battle tomorrow.

1274
01:16:05,858 --> 02:-44:07,942
Shino!

1275
01:17:13,091 --> 02:-43:14,867
You tramp!

1276
01:17:24,436 --> 02:-43:26,222
You wench!

1277
01:17:31,401 --> 02:-43:33,569
Stop this brutality!

1278
01:17:33,737 --> 02:-43:38,074
What the hell is a farmer
girl doing with a samurai?

1279
01:18:03,517 --> 02:-42:05,184
You slut!

1280
01:18:15,320 --> 02:-42:16,704
Manzo.

1281
01:18:17,781 --> 02:-42:19,983
Is this your daughter?

1282
01:18:26,748 --> 02:-42:28,624
Tell me what happened.

1283
01:18:28,792 --> 02:-42:32,029
You mentioned a samurai.
Who was it?

1284
01:18:34,715 --> 02:-42:36,257
Manzo!

1285
01:18:45,976 --> 02:-42:47,810
Manzo, say something.

1286
01:18:48,895 --> 02:-42:50,479
Speak!

1287
01:19:22,846 --> 02:-41:25,014
Are you Shino?

1288
01:19:44,242 --> 02:-41:47,453
Manzo, don't be angry.

1289
01:19:48,914 --> 02:-41:51,999
When the dawn threatens
our very lives,

1290
01:19:52,167 --> 02:-41:55,503
the weight of it makes
us all a little reckless.

1291
01:20:01,343 --> 02:-40:03,886
On the eve of decisive battles...

1292
01:20:05,430 --> 02:-40:08,182
this often happens,
even inside castles.

1293
01:20:11,061 --> 02:-40:15,106
Remember what it was to be young.
You can't blame them.

1294
01:20:16,066 --> 02:-40:18,150
I can't forgive them.

1295
01:20:18,402 --> 02:-40:21,570
I can't stand by when my only daughter
has been made damaged goods.

1296
01:20:36,128 --> 02:-40:40,756
What's wrong with two people in love?
It is not like bandits took her.

1297
01:22:13,183 --> 02:-38:17,336
They are wound up tight.
We need to loosen them up.

1298
01:22:25,529 --> 02:-38:28,781
Everyone, the final battle
is here at last.

1299
01:22:31,785 --> 02:-38:36,038
By the way, Katsushiro,
we expect much of you today.

1300
01:22:37,791 --> 02:-38:40,876
As of last night,
you became a real man.

1301
01:22:58,895 --> 02:-37:00,437
Hey!

1302
01:23:03,400 --> 02:-37:06,527
Where is that fighting spirit?

1303
01:23:08,280 --> 02:-37:11,866
You'll never win
with such long faces!

1304
01:23:25,422 --> 02:-37:27,590
Kikuchiyo, what are you up to?

1305
01:23:27,757 --> 02:-37:30,092
I can't kill five
with just one blade.

1306
01:23:45,775 --> 02:-37:47,693
There are 13 left.

1307
01:23:48,862 --> 02:-37:51,723
We'll let them all in.

1308
01:23:54,409 --> 02:-37:56,827
Once they pass this point,

1309
01:23:57,329 --> 02:-36:01,006
we close in from all
sides at the crossing.

1310
01:24:04,127 --> 02:-36:07,955
Everything is riding
on this battle!

1311
01:24:38,536 --> 02:-36:40,588
Here they come!

1312
01:25:04,104 --> 02:-35:06,055
Here they come!

1313
01:25:30,797 --> 02:-35:33,007
Shichiroji and Katsushiro,
go west!

1314
01:25:33,258 --> 02:-35:35,551
Kyuzo, Kikuchiyo, east!

1315
01:27:17,028 --> 02:-33:19,988
Katsushiro! Rikichi!

1316
01:27:20,156 --> 02:-33:22,825
East! Go east!

1317
01:27:22,992 --> 02:-33:24,868
East!

1318
01:27:41,928 --> 02:-33:43,720
Shut up!

1319
01:27:44,180 --> 02:-33:46,390
Scream and you are dead!

1320
01:28:33,771 --> 02:-32:34,980
We did it!

1321
01:28:35,148 --> 02:-32:36,481
We did it!

1322
01:28:36,649 --> 02:-32:39,401
Head east!

1323
01:28:54,751 --> 02:-32:57,127
Katsushiro, pull back!

1324
01:28:59,631 --> 02:-31:01,882
Damn you!

1325
01:29:03,593 --> 02:-31:05,052
Kikuchiyo!

1326
01:29:41,214 --> 02:-31:43,340
Kikuchiyo!

1327
01:29:53,726 --> 02:-31:56,812
Where are the bandits?

1328
01:29:56,980 --> 02:-31:58,981
They're all dead!

1329
01:30:17,292 --> 02:-30:19,927
Once more we survive.

1330
01:33:57,959 --> 02:-26:00,970
In the end, we lost
this battle too.

1331
01:34:02,892 --> 02:-26:04,142
What?

1332
01:34:04,247 --> 02:-26:05,673
I mean,

1333
01:34:06,979 --> 02:-26:09,664
the victory belongs to those peasants.

1334
01:34:10,128 --> 02:-26:11,762
Not to us.

1335
01:34:13,366 --> 02:-26:17,366
